[31.194827, "o", "Strategy=serendipitous seed=7 latency_ms=29676 tokens~=847\r\n\r\n[SPECULATION: experiment] conf=0.50 nov=0.50 rel=0.80 test=0.90\r\n  The 0.90 novelty score for wandering comes partly from low-frequency memory selection; serendipitous sampling may systematically surface dormant memories that relevant-only retrieval never revisits.\r\n  memories: mem_ed9c580c1f30, mem_df4093e2598a\r\n  experiment: Re-run wandering with serendipitous sampling applied to a stratified subset of memories matched on recency and importance to the relevant-only arm; compare novelty.\r\n\r\n[SPECULATION: prediction] conf=0.60 nov=0.60 rel=0.90 test=0.80\r\n  High novelty reduced in-task relevance, so the wandering agent gains explore-time diversity but may score lower on benchmark correctness measured at answer time.\r\n  memories: mem_ed9c580c1f30, mem_df4093e2598a\r\n  experiment: Score the experiment's generated hypotheses simultaneously on novelty and reference-based correctness to measure the novelty-correctness correlation.\r\n"]
[31.195013, "o", "\r\n[SPECULATION: connection] conf=0.40 nov=0.50 rel=0.70 test=0.80\r\n  The novelty gap may be a labeling artifact: relevant-only retrieval produces hypotheses that resemble prior text in style, while wandering's wider retrieval produces less template-like phrasing that raters score as novel.\r\n  memories: mem_df4093e2598a\r\n  experiment: Ask a second rater set to score novelty blind to retrieval condition, with claude-style paraphrase normalization (topic keywords only) to isolate content novelty.\r\n\r\n[SPECULATION: counterfactual] conf=0.50 nov=0.40 rel=0.80 test=0.90\r\n  Memory sampling strategy interacts with task type: on diverse or open-ended tasks serendipity helps, but on the benchmark's factual items it may hurt, so the \"next week\" comparison might land at parity overall.\r\n  memories: mem_ed9c580c1f30, mem_df4093e2598a\r\n  experiment: Disaggregate the 30-task benchmark by task category and test whether the serendipitous-vs-relevant gap reverses for factual versus open-ended tasks.\r\n\r\n[SPECULATION: experiment] conf=0.50 nov=0.70 rel=0.80 test=0.90\r\n  Chaining serendipitous retrieval directly into the prior turn's relevant retrieval may keep novelty without losing groundedness by combining the parallel retrieval streams at decision time.\r\n  memories: mem_ed9c580c1f30, mem_df4093e2598a\r\n  experiment: Add a third arm to the benchmark mixing relevant + serendipitous retrieval and compare its hypothesis novelty and correctness against both single-strategy arms. All five items are speculative. Supported only by memories mem_ed9c580c1f30 and mem_df4093e2598a; no facts asserted beyond the supplied context.\r\n\r\nGenerated 5 speculative hypothesis/-es. No facts were modified.\r\n"]
[31.246339, "o", "[02:23:30] done\r\n"]
